<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST8802"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Itty<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Itty<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, February 25, 2005 - 9:11 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Hey, Im sorry, I know I am paranoid, but.... <BR>does anyone else find it strange that Tom goes on vacation when this case is really heating up? He is more obesessed with it than us, and he just takes off? So that bothered me...but then on feb 22, in kansas.com, thread called &#34;where is tom v&#34; <BR>he posted one word &#34;bump&#34; <BR><a href="http://forums.prospero.com/n/mb/message.asp?webtag=kr-kansas_news&amp;msg=5948.31" target=_top>http://forums.prospero.com/n/mb/message.asp?webtag =kr-kansas_news&amp;msg=5948.31</a> <BR>Is anyone in San Fran that can check on his home? <BR>What if someone is on his computer? <BR>You can all yell at me now for being so paranoid, but Im serious, I want someone to check on him and his home. Who would you call to do that? <BR>Ed Niel, do you live there?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
